+# ROOT Security Release Notes
+
+## CVE-2025-69650 — binutils (readelf) double free — NOT APPLICABLE (false positive)
+
+- CVE: CVE-2025-69650
+- Package: binutils
+- Shipped version: 2.45.1-r1 (Alpine 3.24)
+- CWE: CWE-415 (Double Free)
+- Status: NOT AFFECTED / FALSE POSITIVE
+- Disposition date: 2026-08-17
+
+### Summary
+
+CVE-2025-69650 describes a double free in GNU Binutils `readelf` reachable via
+the `--got-contents` option: `dump_relocations` may return early without
+initializing the `all_relocations` array, after which
+`process_got_section_contents` passes an uninitialized `r_symbol` pointer to
+`free()`, triggering a SIGABRT (denial of service).
+
+### Why this package is not affected
+
+The vulnerable `--got-contents` subsystem (`update_all_relocations()`,
+`process_got_section_contents()`, and the `all_relocations` state in
+`binutils/readelf.c`) was introduced upstream by commit
+`81e90cf63a10ad11772c2437c8f2a88f1a00c739` on 2025-08-28, which landed only on
+git master and the `binutils-2_46` branch. It is absent from the tagged
+`binutils-2.45.1` release that Alpine 3.24 ships as `2.45.1-r1`. A scan of
+`binutils/readelf.c` in the shipped source confirms zero occurrences of the
+affected functions and state.
+
+The upstream fix commit `ea4bc025abdba85a90e26e13f551c16a44bfa921` (2025-12-08)
+is therefore a no-op against this release — there is no vulnerable code to
+patch. NVD marks CVE-2025-69650 as DISPUTED, noting the behavior occurred only
+in pre-release git-master code and did not affect any tagged Binutils release.
+
+### Resolution
+
+No code change is required or possible. This determination matches the
+dispositions already applied to the Alpine 3.22 and 3.23 binutils packages for
+the same CVE.
